      "raw_mention": "$GOOG",
      "text": "$NOK added AWS, Google Gemini, and Databricks to its autonomous networks platform in the same week. The stock didn't move.\n\nTo understand why this matters, you need to know what Level 4 network autonomy actually means. Right now telecom networks need human engineers to detect problems, diagnose them, and decide what to do. Level 4 is where the network does all of that itself. No ticket, no escalation, no 2am phone call to an on-call engineer.\n\nNokia already has operators running at 90%+ automation rates and getting new services live in under four hours. That used to take weeks.\n\nWhat changed this week is the infrastructure layer behind it. Instead of building their own cloud stack, operators now plug into AWS for compute, Bedrock and SageMaker for AI, Databricks for data, and Gemini for the agent layer. Nokia brings the telecom-trained models that know what a real network fault looks like. AWS and Google bring the scale.\n\nThree of the biggest cloud partnerships in enterprise tech, all announced in seven days. The market is still pricing this with a legacy telecom valuation.\n$NOK $AMZN $GOOG",
